REGEDIT4

; nvgl-on.reg (build 3110): hardware OpenGL for EVERY program, no batch file.
; GALLIUM_DRIVER=nouveau in the "global" application key makes mesa3d.dll (the
; OpenGL ICD) drive the G86's 3D engine through nvmini.vxd for any process that
; creates an OpenGL context. mesa3d.dll reads these keys itself (os_get_option:
; the environment first, then HKLM\Software\vmdisp9x\apps\<exe>\mesa, then
; apps\global\mesa), so hl.exe can simply be started from its folder.
;
; Safety: one process owns the GPU channel at a time (the VxD refuses a second
; one, which then renders in software), and when the hardware screen cannot be
; created the program falls back to software OpenGL instead of getting none.
;
; Per-program opt-out: a value in that program's own key wins over "global":
;   [HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\vmdisp9x\apps\foo.exe\mesa]
;   "GALLIUM_DRIVER"="llvmpipe"
; Everything off again: nvgl-off.reg.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\vmdisp9x\apps\global\mesa]
"GALLIUM_DRIVER"="nouveau"
